WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.046 --> 00:00:04.278
- The moment right before I jump, there's

00:00:04.278 --> 00:00:06.311
a split second there where everything goes

00:00:06.311 --> 00:00:09.230
completely silent, and that's when I push

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.590
off the edge.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:11.448
Three,

00:00:11.448 --> 00:00:12.298
Two,

00:00:12.298 --> 00:00:13.206
One,

00:00:13.206 --> 00:00:14.781
See ya!

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.646
(wind blowing)

00:00:16.646 --> 00:00:17.952
- [Interviewer] Today
I'm speaking with a woman

00:00:17.952 --> 00:00:20.119
who kind of blows my mind.

00:00:20.969 --> 00:00:21.802
(phone ringing)

00:00:21.802 --> 00:00:23.017
- My name is Ellen Brennan, and I'm

00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:24.658
a wingsuit base jumper.

00:00:24.658 --> 00:00:25.931
- [Interviewer] Don't be modest, Ellen.

00:00:25.931 --> 00:00:26.993
What else?

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.928
- [Ellen] Currently I'm
the fastest flying woman

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:32.515
in the world when it comes
to wingsuit base jumping.

00:00:32.515 --> 00:00:34.045
- [Interviewer] A
wingsuit is a special suit

00:00:34.045 --> 00:00:36.371
that inflates with air and
allows you to, in essence,

00:00:36.371 --> 00:00:37.538
fly, or glide.

00:00:39.603 --> 00:00:43.609
Ellen does this all over
the world at crazy speeds.

00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:44.765
- [Ellen] On average I'm flying about

00:00:44.765 --> 00:00:45.765
180-190 kmh.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.729
- [Interviewer] That's almost 120 mph.

00:00:50.729 --> 00:00:54.896
But to get to that speed you
need to jump off a cliff.

00:00:56.754 --> 00:00:58.232
- [Ellen] My vision is
the first thing I notice,

00:00:58.232 --> 00:01:02.399
that everything becomes very
focused on just my speed.

00:01:04.793 --> 00:01:07.301
My heart's beating super
fast, it's usually beating

00:01:07.301 --> 00:01:09.801
like 160-170 beats per minute.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:12.649
Sometimes people will talk to me and I

00:01:12.649 --> 00:01:14.067
won't even hear them.

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:15.598
As soon as I push off, I can hear the slip

00:01:15.598 --> 00:01:18.728
of my feet off of the
rocks, and as I slowly

00:01:18.728 --> 00:01:22.645
start moving I can hear
the wind start to rush.

00:01:24.669 --> 00:01:28.065
(wind blowing)

00:01:28.065 --> 00:01:30.874
(light music)

00:01:30.874 --> 00:01:31.951
- Woo hoo!

00:01:31.951 --> 00:01:34.305
Like, it's something
that shouldn't happen.

00:01:34.305 --> 00:01:37.222
It's not natural, but I'm doing it.

00:01:39.146 --> 00:01:41.030
How in the world did I
get to be able to do that?

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:43.137
It's one of the coolest
things in the world,

00:01:43.137 --> 00:01:46.858
like, I can't think of anything
better to do (laughs).

00:01:46.858 --> 00:01:48.941
It's pretty mind-blowing.

